  "invariants": [
    "HZGCA-OBJ-001 every object type has one authority class and one stable logical ID field",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-002 external canonical references preserve native owning-protocol IDs and are never remapped into competing canonical IDs",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-003 GenerationProject, GenerationIntent, GenerationRunBinding, GenerationOutput, GenerationArtifact and ProvenanceDraft are private by default",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-004 GenerationRunBinding may reference AI/Compute state but cannot rewrite or duplicate its canonical fields",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-005 PublishIntent is explicit user application intent and never proves Work/Recording registration or rights activation",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-006 community Follow/Favorite/Playlist objects do not create 420Commons membership, role or channel authority",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-007 ChartSnapshot and CommunityActivity are derived/rebuildable and never authoritative for rights, awards or payments",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-008 Awards objects are product-domain objects and never Civic governance proposals, ballots or votes",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-009 AwardResult is immutable after finalization and AwardBadge must reference exactly one finalized result",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-010 award prize/payment references are external 420Pay state and cannot alter award legitimacy",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-011 object deletion/tombstone never permits silent ID reuse",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-012 immutable fields cannot be rewritten by later revisions; material semantic changes use explicit version/revision/supersession",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-013 private object identifiers or commitments must not contain plaintext secrets or protected payloads",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-014 Creative CreatorId/WorkId/RecordingId/LicenseId native typed IDs remain authoritative and are referenced directly",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-015 AI and Compute job lifecycles remain owned by their canonical systems; 420Hz stores only binding/observed status metadata",
    "HZGCA-OBJ-016 no object definition grants signing, custody, settlement, governance, identity, rights or dispute authority outside HZ-GCA-1.1 boundaries"
  ],
